-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Gunrunner
  Publisher   Hewson, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Gunrunner (1987)(Hewson Consultants).z80
  MD5         c9d8ff6b87d413df486a42c988c7079e

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. Game logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu,
  are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 set's colours as they are, for the play window only:
              figures, scenery and stars in its 256 colours, the same look on
              every level, the rails taking the level's attribute as the set's
              renderer does. Source: Enhanced colours: Jao Paulo (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: the original game with Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM, no game byte changed in the default; Enhanced: the play
              window in the Spec256 colours on a double-buffered Layer 2, off
              by default; six tested cheats

  Note        Keys: press a key at the picture, then 1 keyboard (M right, N
              left, S up, X down, A fire, Symbol Shift poison, P pause), 2
              Kempston (Space poison), 3 Sinclair or 4 define keys. Default:
              the original game, picture and all: each level's play area is
              one colour on black, so it never had colour clash. Enhanced, on
              the menu, off by default: the play window in the Spec256 set's
              colours on Layer 2; one look for every level. Sinclair's whole
              48K ROM; the 48K game with its beeper sound; fits a 1MB Next.
              Known issues: pace in JNext against the original, 12 runs of 800
              updates in lockstep: whole -1.87 to -0.08%, quiet thirds -1.64
              to -0.07%, busy thirds -2.37 to +0.20%, slowest 20 updates up to
              +6.59%. Missing: in Enhanced the panel, title, menus and level
              text stay in the original colours (the set paints them too; the
              panel's lit items would be lost); natural play past level 1;
              hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  No enemies
   3  Immunity
   4  Infinite poison
   5  Infinite jet pac
   6  Infinite shield

  The archive's POKEs for this release, each tested in the simulator with the
  same keys with and without it: Infinite lives, No enemies and Immunity
  (lives never fall), Infinite poison (three shots leave the count at 3,
  Immunity on in both runs), Infinite jet pac and Infinite shield (the meter
  never falls; the pick-up set by a test poke). None omitted.

